Corrected message:

Paint in-progress strokes beneath the current layer's objects

A stroke being drawn was painted above the current layer's shapes,
text and effect nodes, then dropped beneath them at mouse-up when it
was committed to the layer's raster. It is now painted beneath them
from the start, so it no longer jumps at mouse-up. The colour picker's
pixel sampling reads the same layer order.

Also:
- Toggling a sub-layer's visibility no longer rebuilds the layers
  dock's child rows (which reset the list's scroll position) when the
  row layout is unchanged; the existing rows are refreshed instead.
- The add-in install dialog no longer passes a possibly null parent
  window to its "failed to load" error dialog (CS8604); without a
  parent the error is not shown.
